
Coding rules for the project for AI agents and humans alike.

The project uses TypeScript via JSDoc commments in *.js files with TypeScript
strict mode enabled. Always check the diagnostics for typescript error. The
error can be also checked by running `npm run tsc` command in the terminal.

When you need a helper type or interface, define it in the `types.ts` file.
Those can be referenced globally in the project.

This is a "bundlerless" project. All 3rd deps are in the `vendor` directry and
refeneced via a importmap in the dz/index.html file.

The project uses Preact.js for rendering the UI components. The Components are
written using the `htm` tagged template literal helper to avoid requiring JSX
compilation step.

When referencing a local custom component that takes in props in a `htm` template, use the
use the `h` function from "htm/preact" to render the component. For example:

import { h, html } from "htm/preact";

html`
    ${h(
        Help,
        { label: "?" },
        html`
            <p class="metar" style="font-size: 120%">
                ${cloud.amount}${" "}${cloud.base}${cloud.unit}
            </p>
        `,
    )}
`;


This is to ensure that props are typechecked correctly.
